# tally 2.1.8 item 77 with pick P30 (item 7 of the follow-up): ob's certain take on 2026-04-07 breaks pot whatever oa's
# day in window(04-05, 04-10), but as -160.00 PLN where oa came first and -150.00 PLN where it didn't: the answer is
# what prints, so the plain line is the window's hole (g3), and flows of ob, a leg the refusal reaches, is that hole
# too (g1); each windows each line equals its pinned twin (g2, g4; g5, g6). 2.1.8's first refcore refused every line
# with -150.00 PLN. The review's b4_both_break.
# tally 2.2 (2.2-4): the clause `windows each` is cut; its asks are the plain line, the hole with each unknown day it
# carries named (`unknown day:`, 2.2-11). A caller who takes the window as one day pins its cell.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind savings: place PLN min 0
place pot: savings lives 2025-01-01..
place jar: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input wa: date
input db: date
input amt: money PLN
input small: money PLN
input amt2: money PLN

move oa: transfers
  on wa
  leg cash from pot to jar amount small

move ob: transfers
  on db
  leg cash from pot to world amount amt2

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  small = 10.00 PLN "s"
  amt2 = 200.00 PLN "s"
  wa = window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) "s"
  db = 2026-04-07 "s"
  opening[pot] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"
  opening[jar] = 0.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask g1: flows(ob, 2026-04)
ask g2: flows(ob, 2026-04)
ask g3: bal(pot, 2026-04-30)
ask g4: bal(pot, 2026-04-30)
ask g5: bal(pot, 2026-04-30) with wa = 2026-04-09
ask g6: bal(pot, 2026-04-30) with wa = 2026-04-05
=== expect
g1: ?"date within window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) not precise enough for flows of ob" (oa)
  unknown day: wa
  cut 2026-01-01
g2: ?"date within window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) not precise enough for flows of ob" (oa)
  unknown day: wa
  cut 2026-01-01
g3: ?"date within window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) not precise enough for a balance" (oa)
  unknown day: wa
  cut 2026-01-01
g4: ?"date within window(2026-04-05, 2026-04-10) not precise enough for a balance" (oa)
  unknown day: wa
  cut 2026-01-01
g5: refused: RUN-PLACE pot is -150.00 PLN after the day's observations and plans of 2026-04-07
  pinned: wa = 2026-04-09
  cut 2026-01-01
g6: refused: RUN-PLACE pot is -160.00 PLN after the day's observations and plans of 2026-04-07
  pinned: wa = 2026-04-05
  cut 2026-01-01
warning: WARN-UNREAD input amt is read by nothing
